IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gpa-claims`

-- Government Proceedings Act 1956, ss 4 to 10, 12, 14, 19, 25, 27, 31 and 35 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_government-proceedings-act-1956.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Tort claim fixtures.

`an ordinary negligence claim against a paid officer` MEANS `Tort claim` WITH
    `a private principal would be liable for the officer as agent` IS TRUE
    `the officer would be personally liable` IS TRUE
    `the act was judicial or in executing judicial process` IS FALSE
    `the officer was paid wholly from Government revenues or a certified fund` IS TRUE
    `the act was in exercise of the public duties of the Government` IS FALSE
    `the claim is negligence or trespass in executing construction or maintenance works` IS FALSE
    `s 14 bars the claim` IS FALSE

`an officer who would not be personally liable` MEANS `Tort claim` WITH
